      "[Q28 \u00b7 Technical \u00b7 1 Mark] [GATE 2026 CS1] Consider 2-bit saturating up/down counter for p = 0 and p = 1 respectively.\nFind excitationD 1 andD 0 for the given table.\nFindD 1 andD 0\nCorrect Answer:D 1 = \u00afP Q1 + \u00afP Q0 +Q 1 \u00afQ0,D 0 = \u00afP \u00afQ0 +P \u00afQ1Q0\nSolution:\nStep 1: Understanding the Concept:\nFor D flip-flops, the excitation equation is simply the next-state equation (D=Q +). We use\nthe provided state table to create K-maps forQ +\n1 andQ +\n0 .\nStep 2: Detailed Explanation:\nFrom the table: - **ForD 1 (Q+\n1 ):** The 1s are atP Q 1Q0 \u2208 {001,010,011,111}. - Grouping\nthese in a K-map: - Pair (001,011) gives \u00afP Q0. - Pair (010,011) gives \u00afP Q1. - Pair (011,111)\ngivesQ 1Q0. So,D 1 = \u00afP Q0 + \u00afP Q1 +Q 1Q0.\n22\n- **ForD 0 (Q+\n0 ):** The 1s are atP Q1Q0 \u2208 {000,010,110}. - Grouping: - Pair (000,010) gives\n\u00afP \u00afQ0. - 110 isP Q1 \u00afQ0. So,D 0 = \u00afP \u00afQ0 +P Q1 \u00afQ0.\nStep 3: Final Answer:\nD1 = \u00afP Q1 + \u00afP Q0 +Q 1Q0 andD 0 = \u00afP \u00afQ0 +P Q1 \u00afQ0.\nQuick Tip\nA \"Saturating\" counter doesn't wrap around. Notice that at 11, the next state for an\nup-count (P=0) remains 11, and at 00, the next state for a down-count (P=1) remains",
