      "[Q2 \u00b7 GA \u00b7 1 Mark] [GATE 2026 CS2] Assume that in a certain computer, the virtual addresses are 64 bits long and\nthe physical addresses are 48 bits long. The memory is word addressible. The page\nsize is 8 kB and the word size is 4 bytes. The Translation Look-aside Buffer (TLB)\nin the address translation path has 128 valid entries. At most how many distinct\nvirtual addresses can be translated without any TLB miss?",
